  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">E-Waste Circular Economy Scale: Synergies and Insights</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will catalyze a paradigm shift in e-waste management, transforming it from a linear, wasteful approach to a circular model. It will promote reparability, recovery, recyclability, green employment and partnerships to empower IDPs, refugee, and host communities` self-resilience to drive socio-economic development, transforming them from aid recipients, into self-reliant communities with multiple income streams. This model will include the private sector, whereby displaced populations will be funded to safely repair and recycle e-products in exchange for valuable raw material recovery. The initiative will also provide a unique model for action for UN entities and partners to progress towards achieving the UN goals of climate neutrality and sustainability.</narrative>
  </description>
